```gitignore
# ==============================
# Python
# ==============================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# ==============================
# Virtual Environment
# ==============================
venv/
env/
.venv/
ENV/

# ==============================
# Django
# ==============================
*.log
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
media/
staticfiles/

# Django secret/local settings
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ==============================
# IDE / Editors
# ==============================
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ==============================
# Jupyter Notebook
# ==============================
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ==============================
# Python packaging
# ==============================
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ==============================
# Testing / Coverage
# ==============================
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ==============================
# OS generated files
# ==============================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ==============================
# Temporary files
# ==============================
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak

# ==============================
# Machine learning artifacts
# ==============================
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib

# ==============================
# Large datasets
# Uncomment these if you do NOT
# want datasets pushed to GitHub
# ==============================
# *.csv
# *.xlsx
# *.xls
# *.parquet
# data/

# ==============================
# Node / Frontend (if added later)
# ==============================
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
```

Save it in the **root directory**, beside `manage.py`:

```text
cybersecurity_dashboard/
├── .gitignore
├── manage.py
├── requirements.txt
├── data/
├── cyberdashboard/
└── dashboard/
```

**Important:** I left `.csv` and `data/` *unignored* because your Django dashboard currently reads `data/cybersecurity_attacks.csv`. If the dataset is too large or shouldn't be committed to GitHub, uncomment:

```gitignore
*.csv
data/
```

and keep the dataset locally.
